rch Informatics Program","email":"orrellt@si.edu"},{"last_name":"Informatics and Data Science Center - Digital Stewardship","role":"IPT Administrator","email":"informaticshelp@si.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"32069b11-a9d2-42e2-aa9c-b16350444909","totalCount":9302779,"hitRatio":2.1498952087327885e-7},{"uuid":"1e798b2d-7f97-49b0-a864-79c968af91d3","itemCount":1,"name":"Mississippi Museum of Natural Science Herbarium","description":"The Mississippi Museum of Natural Science Herbarium currently consists of over ~70,000 mounted plant specimens, with approximately 2,000 unmounted specimens in various stages of preparation. Collections from ~29 states are found in the herbarium; however, the majority of the collection (93%) is composed of specimens from Mississippi.","logo":"https://swbiodiversity.org/seinet/content/collicon/MMNS.jpg","url":"http://www.mdwfp.com/seek-study/bio-collections/plants.aspx","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=222","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/mmns_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"heather.sullivan@mmns.state.ms.us"},{"last_name":"Heather Sullivan","email":"heather.sullivan@mmns.state.ms.us"},{"last_name":"Heather Sullivan","email":"heather.sullivan@mmns.state.ms.us"}],"data_rights":"CC3 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":66035,"hitRatio":0.000015143484515787082},{"uuid":"20360fae-574a-4d63-b9f6-47b1cc07fd22","itemCount":1,"name":"Eastern Kentucky University, Ronald L. Jones Herbarium","description":"Several years ago, the Eastern Kentucky University Herbarium (EKY) merged with the Berea College Ralph L. Thompson Herbarium (BEREA) to form a unified collection at Eastern Kentucky University. Both collections are maintained separately in the same physical facilities. As of late 2021, the combined accessioned herbarium collection exceeded 110,000 specimens, and was actively growing. Almost all of the holdings are of vascular plants. This herbarium is by far the largest, most diverse and most active in Kentucky. Significant collections from many people and sources are included in EKY; most of the collections in BEREA are of Ralph Thompson. Significant strengths include Kentucky plants, woody taxa, the Southern Appalachians and Kentucky&rsquo;s Red River Gorge, though there are significant holdings from a much wider area.","logo":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/collicon/eky2.jpg","url":"https://herbarium.eku.edu/","emllink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/collections/datasets/emlhandler.php?collid=193","archivelink":"https://sernecportal.org/portal/content/dwca/eky_dwc-a.zip","contacts":[{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"hbrown@mailbox.sc.edu"},{"email":"sally.chambers@eku.edu"},{"first_name":"Sally","last_name":"Chambers","role":"Curator","email":"sally.chambers@eku.edu"},{"first_name":"Sally","last_name":"Chambers","role":"Curator","email":"sally.chambers@eku.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC3 BY-NC","publisher":"42f2a0a4-5981-4874-88d5-9efb1e8d52c9","totalCount":90387,"hitRatio":0.00001106353789814907},{"uuid":"36d35b23-113e-4633-90ec-19d265a3b5f6","itemCount":1,"name":"The New York Botanical Garden Herbarium (NY)","description":"The William and Lynda Steere Herbarium of The New York Botanical Garden holds a collection of more than seven million preserved specimens. All plant groups – flowering plants, conifers, ferns, mosses, liverworts, and algae, as well as fungi and lichens - are represented in the collection, which is particularly strong in specimens from the Western Hemisphere. Digitization of all groups is ongoing, with ±4.7 million specimens barcoded and ±3.8 million imaged.","logo":"https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/wp-content/themes/nybgscience/images/logo23.svg","url":"https://sweetgum.nybg.org/science/vh/","emllink":"https://sweetgum.nybg.org:8443/ipt/eml.do?r=occurrences","archivelink":"https://sweetgum.nybg.org:8443/ipt/archive.do?r=occurrences","contacts":[{"first_name":"Joel","last_name":"Ramirez","role":"Web Developer for Biodiversity Information Management","email":"jramirez@nybg.org"},{"first_name":"Kimberly","last_name":"Watson","role":"Assistant Director of Biodiversity Information Management","email":"kwatson@nybg.org"},{"first_name":"Leanna","last_name":"Feder","role":"Herbarium Digital Asset Manager","email":"lfeder@nybg.org"},{"first_name":"Elizabeth","last_name":"Gjieli","role":"Geographical Information Manager","email":"egjieli@nybg.org"},{"first_name":"Emily","last_name":"Sessa","role":"Director of the Herbarium","email":"esessa@nybg.org"},{"first_name":"Kimberly","last_name":"Watson","email":"kwatson@nybg.org"},{"first_name":"Kimberly","last_name":"Watson","role":"Assistant Director of Biodiversity Information Management","email":"kwatson@nybg.org"}],"data_rights":"CC0","publisher":"e84b1163-233d-4e46-9eb8-aa2d0d3ff7d8","totalCount":4808642,"hitRatio":2.0795892062665508e-7},{"uuid":"76fd34da-4892-4821-858d-98fe9e28ba8b","itemCount":1,"name":"Valdosta State University Herbarium","description":"The Valdosta State University Herbarium (VSC) provides a repository for the preservation of voucher specimens that document the flora of the Coastal Plain region of Georgia and specimens from a broader geographical area that might be useful in the study of the flora of this region and that enable specialized research on particular groups of plants carried out by faculty and students in residence at Valdosta State University and by taxonomic specialists at other institutions. VSC also provides specimens for use in teaching, and its staff responds to requests from the general public, natural resource managers, agricultural scientists, and others by providing information about plants and service determinations of unknown plants and, where appropriate, preserving vouchers relating to such. In 2009 the Valdosta State University Herbarium established a SQL database, with assistance from the VSU Division of Information Technology, and in 2011 obtained support from the National Science Foundation (DBI 1054366, R. Carter PI) that enabled the purchase of imaging and other digitization equipment and the employment of student assistants to begin capturing images and building a database.  More than 70,000 specimens have been digitized.  In 2012, the Valdosta State University Virtual Herbarium (VSU-VH), a collaborative project between the Herbarium and the VSU Odum Library, was made possible with funding from the Valdosta State University Faculty Research Fund (M. Holt PI, R. Carter Co-PI).  The VSU-VH serves on-line vascular plant specimen images and data, and images and data from more than 4,000 non-vascular plant specimens are served through the Consortium of North American Bryophyte Herbaria (CNABH) portal. \n\n\nVSU Virtual Herbarium http://herb.valdosta.edu/ \n\nConsortium of North American Bryophyte Herbaria http://bryophyteportal.org/portal/index.php","logo":"http://herb.valdosta.edu/redesign/graphics/VState_Metallic_Square_BG.png","url":"http://herb.valdosta.edu/","emllink":"http://herb.valdosta.edu:8080/ipt/eml.do?r=vsu","archivelink":"http://herb.valdosta.edu:8080/ipt/archive.do?r=vsu","contacts":[{"first_name":"Gary","last_name":"Kuhlmann","role":"Webmaster","email":"glkuhlma@valdosta.edu"},{"first_name":"J. Richard","last_name":"Carter","role":"Curator, Professor","email":"rcarter@valdosta.edu"},{"first_name":"J. Richard","last_name":"Carter","role":"Curator, Professor","email":"rcarter@valdosta.edu"},{"first_name":"Michael O","last_name":"Holt","role":"Professor","email":"moholt@valdosta.edu"},{"first_name":"J. Richard","last_name":"Carter","role":"Curator, Professor","email":"rcarter@valdosta.edu"}],"data_rights":"CC4 BY","publisher":"3c49e4fe-de7c-4169-bb3b-c81b1c5a27db","totalCount":68983,"hitRatio":0.000014496325181566473},{"uuid":"beab5209-9628-4d4d-851e-2bc9bb1a0105","itemCount":1,"name":"University of Geo